markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Final Project 

#### At the beginning of this module, you were introduced to the final project, **Value Explorer**, where students apply their learning to design and code that allows users to explore a curated set of opportunities or items.

#### Now that you’ve explored the concepts, you can see how each skill builds toward this culminating experience.

---

<img src="https://images.code.org/fc1f5f35c9a52240d333369516c04017-image-1762456024629.png" alt="miletsone map for project" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 10px 0 0px 10px;">

## Building value explorer app

#### In this project, students act as Front-End Developers and QA Engineers to create an app that explores and compares data.

#### They start by making a plan for their data by mapping out schema fields and work their way through the milestones over the course of 3 days.

#### An  <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1d4NsbpvXnNRYEg9sPOyBlrzCnMIzHX-SJ9lOFb9M9jg/edit?usp=drive_link" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Activity Guide</a> is provided to help keep them organized and on track. 


<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

## Support along the way

<img src="https://images.code.org/068dc84e19b5854c6fd7ae9eaf84e482-image-1767890629612.png" alt="icons for bots that support along the way" width="750px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">

#### Students can choose which tool best supports their current task: brainstorming ideas, organizing their plan, or sketching out their logic and design.

#### 🔁 **Circulate: As students explore the hub, ask guiding questions such as:**
- #### “What type of interaction or outcome are you imagining for your app?”
- ####“Which of these tools will help you move your idea forward right now?”
- ####“How does your planned logic connect to the kind of experience you want your user to have?”

#### Use these check-ins to confirm students are moving from idea to planning, rather than jumping straight into code.

<div style="background-color: #a6e3e8; border-radius: 40px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 1px 20px 1px 20px;">

<p style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 16px; "> <b> 💡Teaching Tip:</b> Set expectations for pacing. Milestone 1 can typically be finished by the end of today's class or early next class. Encourage students to focus first on clarity of idea rather than polish.
</p>
</div>



## You did it! 

#### You’ve now practiced using the tools to build this project while getting an overview of much of the Unit 3 content. This module is designed to give you a strong head start as you prepare to teach the unit.

## Want to try more? 

#### If you’d like to try to complete the full project, open the link in a new tab and return to it after finishing this module.

